1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nf6 5. Nxf6+ exf6 {Book so far. The plan is the usual one: finish development, then decide which side to open.} 6. c3 Bd6 7. Bd3 O-O 8. Qc2 ! h6 {The critical moment. The pieces are as good as they are going to get; something has to happen now.} (8... c5 Rb1 c4 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Ne2 Nd7 10. O-O Re8 11. h3 Nf8 ?! 12. Be3 Be6 13. Nf4 Bxf4 14. Bxf4 Ng6 15. Bxg6 fxg6 16. Qxg6 Bf7 17. Qg3 Kh8 18. b3 a5 19. Qd3 a4 20. c4 Qe7 21. Be3 b5 22. Rfc1 axb3 23. axb3 Rxa1 24. Rxa1 bxc4 25. bxc4 Qe6 26. Ra4 Rb8 27. d5 cxd5 28. c5 Qe8 29. Ra6 Rb4 30. Rb6 Rc4 31. Rd6 h5 32. Kh1 Be6 33. Qb1 Bf7 34. Qb7 Ra4 35. Qb2 Qe4 36. Bd2 Kh7 37. Rd7 Be8 38. Rd8 Bc6 39. Rd6 Be8 40. Rd8 Bc6 41. Rd6 Be8 {The rest is technique, which is another way of saying it still has to be played accurately.} 42. Rd8 1/2-1/2
